t only “$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$.”" 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186329838 1068 17592186329407 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186329838 1068 17592186730164 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186329838 1068 17592186730165 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186329838 1068 17592186730166 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186329838 1068 17592186730167 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186329838 1068 17592186730168 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186329838 1068 17592186730169 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186329838 1071 "![](images/bb/bb8959927fc561f9fc6e021b690c43f4ab57b169aa1526390e02c8d48386bfe3.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the critical points?" 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186329838 1071 "![](images/bb/bb8959927fc561f9fc6e021b690c43f4ab57b169aa1526390e02c8d48386bfe3.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the critical points?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186341964 1068 17592186341581 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186341964 1068 17592186730177 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186341964 1068 17592186730178 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186341964 1068 17592186730179 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186341964 1071 "![](images/43/432991e403167bd560517072d24058c3f2106f093cdcad08f3b5f0ed486f9504.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the critical points?" 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186341964 1071 "![](images/43/432991e403167bd560517072d24058c3f2106f093cdcad08f3b5f0ed486f9504.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the critical points?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186341965 1068 17592186341671 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186341965 1068 17592186730184 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186341965 1068 17592186730185 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186341965 1068 17592186730186 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186341965 1071 "![](images/48/48569328379c72215884b759687c7c40ced06f9864d05d2638e4389694f90630.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the stationary points?" 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186341965 1071 "![](images/48/48569328379c72215884b759687c7c40ced06f9864d05d2638e4389694f90630.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the stationary points?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186600826 1068 17592186600741 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186600826 1068 17592186730180 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186600826 1068 17592186730181 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186600826 1068 17592186730182 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186600826 1068 17592186730183 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186600826 1071 "![](images/99/991ced811f1c8f1e337025b6e2f7273d2b028a3af4a376efb8436956dc40fa62.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the critical points?" 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186600826 1071 "![](images/99/991ced811f1c8f1e337025b6e2f7273d2b028a3af4a376efb8436956dc40fa62.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the critical points?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186600837 1068 17592186600778 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186600837 1068 17592186730174 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186600837 1068 17592186730175 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186600837 1068 17592186730176 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186600837 1071 "![](images/36/36477ec421ff4b7f349a060df762eadee83b008fbfc9e021a8893cc45e405cae.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. $f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=2$\n\nII. $f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=-2$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=-2$" 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186600837 1071 "![](images/36/36477ec421ff4b7f349a060df762eadee83b008fbfc9e021a8893cc45e405cae.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186600837 1074 "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(2)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=-2$ since $f(-2)\\ge f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough  to $x=-2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a sharp edge at $x=-2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(-2)$ does not exist.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186600837 1074 "Let's check our statements.\n\n- The statement “$f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=2$” is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(2)=0.$\n\n- The statement “$f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=-2$” is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=-2$ since $f(-2)\\ge f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough  to $x=-2.$\n\n- The statement “$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=-2$” is false. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a sharp edge at $x=-2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(-2)$ does not exist.\n\nTherefore, select “$f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=2$” and “$f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=-2$.”" 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186620891 1068 17592186620807 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186620891 1068 17592186730160 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186620891 1068 17592186730161 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186620891 1068 17592186730162 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186620891 1068 17592186730163 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186620891 1071 "![](images/da/daba5c9c96666b81c5e0e3c0623aa97e234b208dc90f9a3f57785bfcc17552d9.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. Given that $f(x)$ is defined on the interval $x\\in [-10,2]$, which points represent the global minimum of $f(x)?$" 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186620891 1071 "![](images/da/daba5c9c96666b81c5e0e3c0623aa97e234b208dc90f9a3f57785bfcc17552d9.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. Given that $f(x)$ is defined on the interval $x\\in [-10,2]$, which points represent the global minimum of $f(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729422 1146 17592186340002 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186729422 1146 17592186730148 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729422 1146 17592186730149 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729422 1146 17592186730151 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729440 1146 17592186340531 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186729440 1146 17592186730133 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729440 1146 17592186730136 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729440 1146 17592186730137 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729498 1146 17592186328322 13194139543292 17592186576411 false] [17592186729498 1146 17592186730107 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729498 1146 17592186730110 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729498 1146 17592186730111 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729498 1146 17592186730114 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729498 1146 17592186730115 13194139543292 17592186576411 true] [17592186729498 1146 17592